      "id": "2121774637931475331",
      "lang": "en",
      "note_tweet": {
        "text": "…yeah but designing their own chips alone doesn’t mean they can compete with Nvidia. People were designing their own chips before all of these but Nvidia had structural advantages (e.g. know-how, Jensen’s supply chain relationship etc) but Jalapeño style model-ASIC co-design (+AI-assisted design) was a game changer that basically forced Nvidia to do neocloud + open weight play (though I think he also liked the idea of open weight). The gambit is basically to redraw & cement supply chain layers of the new industry in a way that disincentivize co-design. All signs are pointing toward this (e.g. HF acquisition, rumor that Nvidia is training frontier class open weight etc) and would’ve worked depending on the timeline… but now we’re entering a new timeline unfortunately."
      },
